course: dictionary
lesson: 1219
title: Builders and building
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A builder is a person whose job is to build or repair houses and other buildings. The word comes from the verb build with -er on the end, and -er often means "a person who does this." «In a community people do different jobs: farmers grow food, doctors treat illness, teachers teach, builders build.» Here builders are one job among many, and the sentence shows what each job does.
explain: Builder can also mean anything that builds something. A bird can be a nest builder, and you can be a Lego builder. «Most builders have to try many times before a model works.» Here builders are people who make models. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "Most people who make things have to try many times" still makes sense.
explain: The words around a word give clues. «For centuries most people learned jobs as apprentices, living and working with a master for years, while guilds of bakers, weavers and builders set the rules.» Bakers and weavers are trades, so builders must be people who do a trade too. Read on to find the clues before you reach for a dictionary.
fact: A builder is a person whose job is to build or repair houses and other buildings.
fact: The ending -er often means "a person who does this": build becomes builder, teach becomes teacher.
fact: Builder can also mean anything that builds something, such as a nest builder or a Lego builder.
fact: Building sites can be dangerous, with holes, machines and falling objects, so builders wear hard hats and high-visibility jackets.
fact: «A team of builders» means a group of people who build together, and «confidence builder» means something that makes you feel more sure of yourself.
exercise: In «doctors treat illness, teachers teach, builders build», what is a builder's job? | Treating sick people | Growing food on a farm | Teaching in a school | *Building or repairing houses and other buildings
exercise: Which of these is a builder in the sense of anything that builds? | A tall tree | A cup of hot cocoa | *A bird that builds a nest | A lamp that gives out light
exercise: The -er at the end of builder usually means what? | A type of food | *A person who does the action | A colour | Something that is broken
test: «Most builders have to try many times before a model works.» What does this sentence tell you about builders? | They never need to try a second time | They only build with sand | They always finish in one go | *They often try again and again until something works
test: Why do builders wear hard hats on a building site? | Because hats keep them warm in the summer | *Because the site has holes, machines and falling objects | Because hats are fashionable | Because they are playing a game
exam: Which sentence uses builder to mean a person whose job is building? | A confidence builder helps you feel brave | *The team of builders put a new roof on the school | The bird is a nest builder | Lego builders make towers
